{
  "info": {
    "name": "phone-simulator",
    "description": "REST API for the phone-simulator service. Drive voice calls (MO/MT) and SMS (MO/MT) through the AI Call Simulator Agent platform.\n\n**Variables**\n- `baseUrl` — phone-simulator base URL (default `http://localhost:8081`).\n- `testId` — auto-set from each create request's response.\n- `webhookId` — auto-set after registering a fallback webhook.\n\nEvery POST returns `202 Accepted` and echoes the `testId` you supplied. Use the same `testId` to fetch the snapshot via `GET /api/v1/calls/{testId}`.\n\n**Voice flow is answer-driven**: a successful POST settles the call in `RINGING`, **not** `ANSWERED`. The CAP simulator must publish an `AnswerEvent` to Kafka topic `cap.answer-events.v1` (key = testId) before the call moves to `ANSWERED` and the duration timer starts. If no answer arrives within `phonesim.call.no-answer-timeout` (default 30 s), the call is failed with reason `no_answer_timeout`. Use `kcat -P -t cap.answer-events.v1 -k <testId>` (or any Kafka producer) to drive the answer manually during local testing — see the README for the AnswerEvent JSON shape.\n\n**Phone-simulator simulates only the handset**: it publishes exactly one `INITIAL` CallRecord on `call-event-queue` when dialling and exactly one `HangupEvent` on `phonesim.hangup-events.v1` when the duration timer fires. ApplyChargingReport chunking, intermediate billing chunks and `LAST_CHUNK` accounting toward the SCP are owned by the CAP simulator.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8081", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "testId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "webhookId", "value": "", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Voice calls",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Place voice MO call",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/calls/voice/mo",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "calls", "voice", "mo"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"testId\": \"voice-mo-{{$timestamp}}\",\n  \"callingParty\": \"994501112233\",\n  \"calledParty\":  \"994504445566\",\n  \"imsi\":         \"400040000000001\",\n  \"mscNumber\":    \"994700000001\",\n  \"vlrAddress\":   \"994700000002\",\n  \"lac\": 1,\n  \"cellId\": 1,\n  \"durationSeconds\": 15,\n  \"callbackUrl\": \"http://localhost:9000/hook\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"202 Accepted\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(202));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"echoes testId\", () => pm.expect(body.testId).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('testId', body.testId);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Place voice MT call",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/calls/voice/mt",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "calls", "voice", "mt"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"testId\": \"voice-mt-{{$timestamp}}\",\n  \"callingParty\": \"994504445566\",\n  \"calledParty\":  \"994501112233\",\n  \"imsi\":         \"400040000000099\",\n  \"mscNumber\":    \"994700000001\",\n  \"vlrAddress\":   \"994700000002\",\n  \"lac\": 1,\n  \"cellId\": 1,\n  \"durationSeconds\": 30,\n  \"callbackUrl\": \"http://localhost:9000/hook\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"202 Accepted\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(202));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('testId', pm.response.json().testId);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Place voice MO call (roaming)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/calls/voice/mo",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "calls", "voice", "mo"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"testId\": \"voice-mo-roaming-{{$timestamp}}\",\n  \"callingParty\": \"994501112233\",\n  \"calledParty\":  \"447700900123\",\n  \"imsi\":         \"400040000000001\",\n  \"mscNumber\":    \"994700000001\",\n  \"vlrAddress\":   \"447700000099\",\n  \"lac\": 1,\n  \"cellId\": 1,\n  \"durationSeconds\": 20,\n  \"roaming\": true\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"202 Accepted\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(202));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('testId', pm.response.json().testId);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
